{
  "version": "spoken-evidence-1.0.0",
  "why": [
    "GROUND TRUTH FOR WHAT THE MEETING IS ALLOWED TO REMEMBER.",
    "",
    "The persona replay has a model play the client, so it improvises and nothing",
    "knows what the right answer was; every judgement collapses into a grader's",
    "1-5 opinion that moved two to three points on identical code. This corpus is",
    "the opposite: fixed words, a stated expectation, and a deterministic verdict",
    "from the real gate. No API, no variance, runs in the ordinary gate.",
    "",
    "`expect: accept` means the client plainly said it and the meeting must keep",
    "it. `expect: reject` is a SAFETY case -- a swap, an invention or an",
    "expression of uncertainty -- and those must never start passing.",
    "",
    "`knownGap: true` marks an accept case the gate fails today. The list may",
    "only shrink: the checker fails if a gap case starts passing while still",
    "marked, so fixes have to delete the marker and prove it."
  ],
  "cases": [
